Size the JPEG CAPTURE buffer against the real worst case on a 64 MB part.

ak_venc_cap_size() sizes a JPEG CAPTURE buffer as the full raw frame
(width * height * 3 / 2) even though the comment above it documents the
worst case as about half that. On the 64 MB AK3918EV200 the coherent
pool is roughly 18 MB; with main capture holding four YUV420 buffers
and the H.264 encoder its output buffers, the MJPEG encoder's third
context cannot allocate a full-size JPEG CAPTURE buffer and
VIDIOC_REQBUFS fails with -ENOMEM. Half the raw frame still leaves
ample room for a 1280x720 baseline JPEG (observed frames are ~80 KB).

--- a/drivers/media/platform/anyka/ak-venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/anyka/ak-venc.c
@@ -1110,7 +1110,7 @@ static unsigned ak_venc_cap_size(u32 fourcc, unsigned width, unsigned height)
 	if (fourcc != V4L2_PIX_FMT_JPEG)
 		return ak_venc_bitstream_size(width, height);
 
-	size = width * height * 3 / 2;
+	size = width * height * 3 / 4;
 	if (size < AK_VENC_MIN_BITSTREAM)
 		size = AK_VENC_MIN_BITSTREAM;
 	return ALIGN(size, 8);
